Splash
Splashboard is a front end for Splash (https://github.com/incoai/splash), the local
inference engine for Apple silicon by inco.ai, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. Splash is not bundled in the app: users install it from Homebrew
(incoai/tap/splash). The test stand-in in scripts/fake_splash contains files copied
from Splash 1.3.0 and files derived from it; scripts/fake_splash/NOTICE lists them,
and scripts/fake_splash/LICENSE.splash is Splash's license.
Splashboard is not an official inco.ai product, and is not endorsed by inco.ai.

Other third-party software
It bundles the Archivo typeface (SIL Open Font License 1.1).
The packaged app also bundles CPython 3.13 (Python Software Foundation License,
from python-build-standalone) and the Python packages it depends on. Each keeps
its own license, and licenses/THIRD_PARTY.txt in the app reproduces their texts.
The web admin also ships Preact, @preact/signals, wouter-preact, uPlot, marked and
highlight.js (MIT, Unlicense and BSD-3-Clause). Their license texts are not in
THIRD_PARTY.txt yet.
The runtime's native code is not covered by THIRD_PARTY.txt either: OpenSSL 3.5.9,
expat 2.8.5, bzip2 1.0.8, libmpdec, libffi, HACL*, SQLite, liblzma, and Tcl and Tk
9.0.4 with their itcl and thread extensions. Their license texts are not in the app
yet.
